[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2659569163","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102860#issuecomment-2659569163","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102860","id":2659569163,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ehc4L","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-14T15:06:01Z","updated_at":"2025-02-14T15:06:46Z","body":"I can confirm this on 4.4.beta b607110ad211778a6426a00ca9c8cd99c0eb383c (Linux, GeForce RTX 4090 with NVIDIA 565.77). This occurs whenever **Scaling 3D Scale** is set to a value other than `1.0`, likely because this engages different shader defines (scaling is only performed when needed to save resources in Compatibility).\n\nPS: Setting **Scaling 3D Scale** above 2.0 will not look any better than 2.0, because Godot does not implement advanced downsampling shaders. Bilinear scaling is limited to 2.0 before it gets grainy and doesn't actually improve quality.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2659569163/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676007618","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102860#issuecomment-2676007618","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102860","id":2676007618,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fgKLC","user":{"login":"Namey5","id":38927424,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTI3NDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38927424?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5","html_url":"https://github.com/Namey5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Namey5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T04:35:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T04:35:04Z","body":"Can confirm this difference occurs between any two scenarios that involve drawing directly to the backbuffer vs. drawing to an intermediate buffer (eg. enabling 'glow' or 'adjustments' in the environment also exhibits this).\n\nIt looks like when not using an intermediate buffer, the tonemapping is handled directly in the draw shaders themselves (which makes sense, but in this case would mean the 'custom clear color' background will only ever receive tonemapping when done in post). The 3D scene should in theory be the same though, so I'm wondering if either:\n\n1. The tonemapping is *always* being applied in the scene shader, thus scene objects receive tonemapping twice when using an intermediate buffer.\n2. There is some weird colour-space difference between the scene shader vs. post effect.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2676007618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3395376296","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102860#issuecomment-3395376296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102860","id":3395376296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7KYVSo","user":{"login":"Kaleb-Reid","id":78945904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4OTQ1OTA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78945904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid","html_url":"https://github.com/Kaleb-Reid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kaleb-Reid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-12T21:24:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-12T21:25:28Z","body":"I didn't notice a difference in the scene on master, so I'm guessing I fixed that with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110915 which fixed tonemapping happening twice in some cases after toggling settings on and then off again. The clear colour on the other hand, is still broken which should be fixed by #111550.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3395376296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5172504583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102860#issuecomment-5172504583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102860","id":5172504583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNE4oBw","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-03T22:40:23Z","updated_at":"2026-08-03T22:40:23Z","body":"Can confirm in 4.7.1","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/